From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:14:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Expand patch diff previews when configured

Base: openai/codex rust-v0.159.2 ff6aec96948b70d94983af2641a6b67c94faeff5
Prerequisite: base-configuration/codex-unleashed-configuration.patch

Own the expanded_diff_previews property and stable default-on feature flag.
Use the shared configuration table without introducing another feature's
runtime properties or behavior. The property remains false by default.

Verification (Rust 1.95.0, RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216):
- cargo test -p codex-config --lib codex_unleashed: 2 passed.
- cargo test -p codex-core --lib codex_unleashed: all selected tests pass.
- Full-queue schema CLI equality and owned-transcript configuration checks
  verify the extracted declaration composes with both feature patches.

Release-base compatibility: the rust-v0.160.0 thread-manager sample initializes this project property to its existing false default. The full workspace compile identifies the missing field before this repair.
